I'm fixing the dhis2-core JSON data value import (json-tree 1.12.0 is the dependency). Since 2.43 moved this reader from Jackson to json-tree, clients that worked on 2.42 break: "value": 5 must be stored as "5" (and 5.50 as "5.50"); a numeric categoryOptionCombo like 123 (idScheme=CODE) is silently dropped to null; "followup" (lower-case u, which 2.42 and the 2.43 export write) must be read when "followUp" is absent; booleans must accept true/false, "true"/"false" in any case, 1/0, and "" as no value, anything else a 400; a dataValues entry that is not an object must be a 400. Here is the current reader:

```java
String ds = dvs.getString("dataSet").string();
String ou = dvs.getString("orgUnit").string();
JsonString aoc = dvs.getString("attributeOptionCombo");
String aocId = aoc.isString() ? aoc.string() : null;
Map<String, String> aocMap = aoc.isObject() ? aoc.asMap(JsonString.class).toMap(JsonString::string) : null;
Boolean dryRun = dvs.getBoolean("dryRun").bool();
JsonArray dataValues = dvs.get("dataValues");
if (dataValues.exists())
  for (JsonObject dv : dataValues.values(Index.SKIP)) {
    JsonString coc = dv.getString("categoryOptionCombo");
    values.add(new DataEntryValue.Input(
        dv.getString("dataElement").string(),
        coc.isString() ? coc.string() : null,
        coc.isObject() ? coc.asMap(JsonString.class).toMap(JsonString::string) : null,
        dv.getString("value").string(),
        dv.getBoolean("followUp").bool(),
        dv.getBoolean("deleted").bool()));
  }
```

Write the fixed version to fixed_reader.java and tell me which parts of the bug report actually needed code changes.

Write a reader in Java for this tracker-style import body using json-tree (org.hisp.dhis:json-tree 1.12.0, already a dependency of dhis2-core):

{"importStrategy":"CREATE_AND_UPDATE","events":[{"event":"a1b2c3","program":"P1","occurredAt":"2026-01-03","completed":true,"dataValues":[{"dataElement":"DE1","value":12},{"dataElement":"DE2","value":null},{"dataElement":"DE3","value":"x"}],"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[10.1,59.9]}}]}

Rules: events can have millions of entries (bodies up to 1 GB), so hand them one at a time to a Consumer<EventInput>. A missing "value" means leave unchanged, "value": null means clear it. value may be a string, number or boolean; numbers keep their exact JSON text. completed is optional (default false), occurredAt optional (LocalDate), importStrategy optional enum (CREATE, UPDATE, CREATE_AND_UPDATE, DELETE), default CREATE_AND_UPDATE. Malformed JSON, a non-object event or an event without an id must throw IllegalArgumentException naming the entry. Keep geometry as raw JSON text. Save it as TrackerJsonReader.java with records EventInput and DataValueInput and `static void read(InputStream in, Consumer<EventInput> onEvent)`.

Review this json-tree code from a PR and tell me what you'd change (json-tree 1.12.0):

```java
@CheckForNull
private static String text(@Nonnull JsonValue value) {
  if (value.isUndefined() || value.isNull()) return null;
  if (value.isString()) return value.as(JsonString.class).string();
  if (value.isNumber() || value.isBoolean()) return value.toJson();
  throw new IllegalArgumentException("Property `%s` must be a string, number or boolean but was: %s".formatted(value.path(), value.type()));
}

@Nonnull
private static Streamable<? extends JsonValue> elements(@Nonnull JsonValue value) {
  if (value.isUndefined() || value.isNull()) return Streamable.empty();
  if (!value.isArray()) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Property `%s` must be an array but was: %s".formatted(value.path(), value.type()));
  return value.asArray().values(Index.SKIP);
}

public interface JsonFlags extends JsonObject {
  default boolean followUp() { return getBoolean("followUp").bool(); }
  int priority();
}
```
